4163ff016a36377d9f18a56f2f00becb0c23fc1c28e839cbd9dc38cd301dd353 1791169095 First entry of the map-engine log. From this commit, the repository keeps its history in log/events.log and the frozen artifacts of log/artifacts/, and it is ready to be public. Base: the branch v0.0.7 at commit 4988cfe, package version 0.0.7. The artifact ca024dad78fe1c4c8a41bbddb88209ab6c451bd3b98a461c1070752df1a95867.tar.gz in log/artifacts/ is a git archive of commit 4988cfe, with 66 files under the prefix map-engine-4988cfe/. It holds the development of map-engine from the first commit on 2026-04-06 to 4988cfe on 2026-07-22, 78 commits: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/ (9 rules, the settings, and 2 skills), .mcp.json, CHANGELOG.md with its 0.0.7 section, the README.md of 4988cfe (577 lines), and docs/. docs/ holds vision.md, 8 research files, and the archive of 40 files: its README, the roadmap, its traceability matrix, 5 phase audits, the PRD, the progress file, and the epics of each version from v0.0.1 to v0.0.6, and the v0.0.7 plan REGISTRY-SCAN-FOOTPRINT-PLAN.md. Its name is the sha256 of its bytes, and a second git archive of the same 66 paths gives the same hash. CLAUDE.md as it stood at 4988cfe is frozen in this artifact, with .claude/ and AGENTS.md, which was a link to CLAUDE.md. From this entry, AGENTS.md at the root is the canonical agent file, and CLAUDE.md at the root holds only the line @AGENTS.md, so that Claude Code loads it. Why: until this commit, the plans, the agent files, the changelog, and the README were mutable documents. Each edit overwrote the last state, and nothing kept the path that led to it. From this commit, each commit adds one line to log/events.log, no line changes, and material from outside is a frozen artifact that a line names by its hash. The snapshot keeps the old documents as they were, so the tree no longer carries them. Changes to the tree: the 65 legacy files leave the tree, README.md is new, AGENTS.md is new and lean, and CLAUDE.md points to it. The README is short, for a new reader: what the engine is, a screenshot (docs/example.png), install, minimal use, the API in brief, the example and the tests, the limits, the development log, and the license. docs/REFERENCE.md holds the old README with its links fixed, the v0.0.7 load-time and memory figures, and pointers into the snapshot for vision.md and the roadmap. LICENSE is MIT. package.json adds the license, a description, keywords, the files list, an optional peer @types/three, a prepare script so that a git install builds dist, and the scripts check:log and commit. npm test also runs test/event-log.node.ts under node --test. tsconfig.build.json sets declarationMap false. Each line of log/events.log is <id> <time> <body>: the id is the sha256 of the body as stored, the time is the Unix time in seconds, and the body escapes a backslash, a line feed, a carriage return, and a tab. A commit adds exactly one line, and a merge commit keeps every line of each parent and adds one line. .gitattributes merges log/events.log with the union driver, so branches merge and rebase with no conflict, and .gitignore exempts log/ from *.log. scripts/commit.ts escapes the body, files each artifact under its hash, adds the line, and commits, and scripts/event-log.ts holds the format for it and for scripts/check-log.ts. scripts/check-log.ts checks the format, the artifacts, and the commit rule from the first commit that holds log/events.log, because the 78 earlier commits have no line. The engine changes on top of v0.0.7, with no version change: the camera methods getView, setView, and fitBounds with the fit option (experimental), touch pan and pinch zoom, the viewChange event, getSectorId and getSectorKey, MapConfig.ignoredColors (experimental), and WorkerStartError. loadMap() can run again after a failed load. dispose() during a load rejects it with MapInvalidatedError, and dispose() and destroy() reject the calls in flight. The Worker starts at the first loadMap(). The build uses a relative base and stripInternal, and npm run build and npm test check dist with bin/check-dist.mjs, bin/check-dist-types.mjs, and bin/check-dist-test.mjs. package.json sets no sideEffects field: with sideEffects false, the bundler dropped the module that registers the pathfinding handlers, and the built worker rejected setTraversalCosts and findPath. bin/check-dist.mjs now fails when a handler that src/worker registers is not in the built worker. The example app adds a camera feature. bench/quickstart-verify.spec.ts polls up to 5 s for the map-mode recolor in place of a fixed wait of 100 ms, which failed one of its 2 cases on the v0.0.7 tip on a slow machine. Four lines that named a legacy file, in bench/SPEC.md and three test files, now point to the snapshot or name no file. Checked: npm ci, npm run typecheck, typecheck:example, typecheck:bench, and typecheck:test exit 0, npm test passes 398 of 398 in 38 files, 12 check-dist cases, and 53 event log tests, npm run build and build:example exit 0, npm run size gives 16341 bytes, npm run check:log, npm run bench:verify, and npm pack --dry-run exit 0 with 38 files, and npm run verify:quickstart passes 2 of 2. Open: the repository field of package.json, and a version for the release.
